cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "PeerReviewAgents"
abstract: >-
  PeerReviewAgents produces an evidence-linked peer review of a manuscript PDF.
  One command imports the PDF locally into immutable source blocks, then runs a
  Claude Code plugin workflow over them: several core reviewers and six
  specialist tracks work in parallel and in isolation, and an editor pools what
  they found into one package with a decision and a reason for every finding.
  The plugin's own server owns the manuscript, the agent identities, the tool
  allowances, the budgets and the run files, so no agent's account of its own
  work is taken on trust. Every finding carries the source block it is anchored
  to and the exact quotation it rests on; a quotation that does not match the
  manuscript is quarantined rather than reported, and the server, not the
  agent, decides whether a finding rests on arithmetic over printed values, on
  a second corroborating quotation, or on judgment. Reviews run on a signed-in
  Claude Code subscription and make no API-key calls. Each run records its
  manuscript manifest, stage ledger, provenance hashes, per-agent models and
  token usage, and the reports are written from that saved JSON without further
  inference, so a stopped or blocked run still reports what it produced. The
  system is research software for review assistance and evaluation, not a
  substitute for accountable editorial judgment.
type: software
